cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "covariogram-explorer: exact covariograms of planar shapes in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gasparyan"
    given-names: "Manvel"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    affiliation: "Ghent University Global Campus"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/manvelgasparyan/covariogram-explorer"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for the exact covariograms g(x) = area of K ∩ (K + x) of
  planar shapes (disk, ellipse, annulus, Reuleaux triangle, parallelograms,
  triangles and convex polygons), the distributions of distances between random
  points and of chord lengths derived from them, the covariogram of binary
  images, and an interactive explorer with a gallery of shapes.
keywords:
  - covariogram
  - set covariance
  - geometric probability
  - stochastic geometry
  - mathematical morphology
  - Reuleaux triangle
  - random distances
  - interactive visualization
references:
  - type: unpublished
    authors:
      - family-names: "Gasparyan"
        given-names: "Manvel"
    title: "An explicit formula for the covariogram of the Reuleaux triangle"
    year: 2026
    notes: "Submitted manuscript"
